#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c942d3-63a4-59a3-b6d0-9aa7ddba1439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-5)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327087} {:answer/id #uuid "49403a97-405f-5f84-96e2-5b992bd4eab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327572} {:answer/id #uuid "748c09d4-9a5f-51d6-ba16-a446207f2ee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-5)\\cup (5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327937} {:answer/id #uuid "74a46401-9b4e-5abc-9a97-e45d5b010ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327938} {:answer/id #uuid "fc47eef6-da40-5792-aae8-9d2421e2e586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49403a97-405f-5f84-96e2-5b992bd4eab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327572} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7213bfa-2e48-5cbc-80d5-fc5e4597837b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329505}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43671ef1-4b81-53b4-8687-766126e69d47" :question/math-academy-id "q-44625" :question/problem "For which values of $x$ is ${x}^{2}-5x>0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x & >0 \\\\ x(x-5) & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $x(x-5)=0.$ The roots are $x=0$ and $x=5,$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,0),$ $(0,5),$ and $(5,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $(0,5)$ | $(5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-5$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x(x-5)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(+)\\cdot (-)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $x(x-5)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $x(x-5)$ is positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(5,\\infty ).$ \nTherefore, we conclude that ${x}^{2}-5x>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (5,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "826552d3-c4e0-538c-9196-4afb18110140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248579} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf08c39-e90f-5ba4-9229-d2ffff374c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-13)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248811} {:answer/id #uuid "9fb2522e-32d2-56e6-ac37-54a4312dd677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (13,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248847} {:answer/id #uuid "af81a493-1449-5b36-ab97-412b7aebe26d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-13)\\cup (13,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248998} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1caebc-93ec-52f4-b0af-a5dbfeb7b5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-13,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce1caebc-93ec-52f4-b0af-a5dbfeb7b5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-13,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249251} :answer-field/id #uuid "faa7acea-63e1-5f4b-ad99-c211d52b1202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250113}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2bb17ed-6922-578d-aad8-d1768d7a7b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115426" :question/problem "For which values of $x$ is ${x}^{2}+13x<0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+13x & <0 \\\\ x(x+13) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $x(x+13)=0.$ The roots are $x=-13$ and $x=0,$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,-13),$ $(-13,0),$ and $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-13)$ | $(-13,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+13$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x(x+13)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(+)\\cdot (-)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $x(x+13)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $x(x+13)$ is negative.\n\nWe see that the expression is negative on the interval $(-13,0).$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that ${x}^{2}+13x<0$ for all $x\\in (-13,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11111aea-53ef-566e-8d48-b22714b81ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247575} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9155ea-8e61-5304-b495-ca30e612c92a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-11,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249090} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc6ae26-25e4-5d79-b8ea-0b6ceef59f6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (11,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249243} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf07fa4-5360-5e71-9f42-96c78eafdae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (11,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249249} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2c78f4-7db5-5b6b-bcbe-6e6698238630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2c78f4-7db5-5b6b-bcbe-6e6698238630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249370} :answer-field/id #uuid "11b7aaf8-8904-5892-a8bc-99889f1ec532" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249700}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9a349ab-e44f-5a1f-9f97-ccc234b5cc72" :question/math-academy-id "q-115864" :question/problem "For which values of $x$ is ${x}^{2}+11x>0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+11x & >0 \\\\ x(x+11) & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $x(x+11)=0.$ The roots are $x=-11$ and $x=0$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,-11),$ $(-11,0),$ and $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x(x+11)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(-)\\cdot (+)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $x(x+11)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $x(x+11)$ is positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-11)$ and $(0,\\infty ).$ \nTherefore, we conclude that ${x}^{2}+11x>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186